Carry terrestrial Output's Location branch in its actor definition

Dev accepted, in these words: "re-author Output's message as a case branch binding location to
domains.terrestrial.Location, with the three strict bindings and consumer(report), the report
constructed in the OriginateReport form, Output.scala regenerated from the definition, and one
OutputProjectionTest covering exact trio agreement, one report per Location, ignored other
messages and lazy consumer capture." Output was the one example difference the October audit
found to be more than spelling: its drake message body read `location` that nothing bound — the
hand-written `case location: Location =>` and its catch-all had never reached the definition —
and constructed the report as `LocationReport(typeDefinition:…, json:payload)`, a named
construction of a type with no factory, which the engine passes through unmapped and Scala has
no apply to meet. The generated file could not compile either way.

The message body is now one branch, `case location Location [ … ]`, the branch type spelled bare
because Location is in Output's own package, holding `now fix payload` (the same io.circe.Json.obj
tree), `now fix report LocationReport new LocationReport { … }` — host text, the form the
terrestrial OriginateReport rule has carried since 97bf690 — and `mon consumer(report)`. Two
bindings, not three: the accepted wording counted the consumer line. The JSON is re-canonicalized
from the drake with the compiled DrakeCLI (surface drift 0, json drift 0 over terrestrial) and
Output.scala is the compiled GeneratorCLI's output, unscoped as the other example actors were
regenerated: it dispatches `case location: Location =>` with the generator's `case _ => ()`, binds
the two values strictly, and takes the Terrestrial actor convention the hand-written file lacked —
`elementTypeNames` and a `knowledge` registering the domain's ConsumeReport and OriginateReport
rules, exactly as Creator and the terrestrial Consumer carry them. No engine change. LocationReport
keeps no factory, so its construction stays host text; a `json` factory on it, which would let
Output and OriginateReport both construct through the named-argument path, was named as adjacent
and is not recommended here.

OutputProjectionTest (4) is new, the 73rd suite, on the ConsumerProjectionTest pattern: exact
drake/JSON/Scala agreement with the World actor role; each Location producing one LocationReport
whose payload carries type LOCATION, latitude, longitude and elevationMetres in that order, the
report's typeDefinition being LocationReport's; Observable and Position ignored before and after
an accepted Location; the consumer captured lazily, once per actor, with signals inert.

